# 7. This gives us a proper Kernel reduction theorem

We can formulate the research target as:

> **Kernel Minimality Candidate Theorem**
>
> Let \(\mathcal K_0\) be a candidate Kernel whose responsibilities preserve all mandatory requirements \(\mathcal R_{\rm req}(Q,\Gamma)\). A component \(c\in\mathcal K_0\) is Kernel-essential only if its removal causes failure of at least one mandatory Kernel invariant and the responsibility cannot be reconstructed from the remaining structure.

Formally:

$$
\boxed{
Essential(c)
\iff
Necessary(c)
\land
Irreducible(c)
\land
NonReconstructible(c)
}
$$

Then:

$$
\boxed{
\mathcal K_{\min}
=
\mathcal K_0
\setminus
\{c:\neg Essential(c)\}
}
$$

subject to proving that the resulting structure still satisfies every Kernel obligation.

