# 8. And now we can connect this to the probabilistic space

This is where your earlier question becomes particularly interesting.

We should **not** define:

$$
\mathcal K= \mathfrak P(\mathfrak E).
$$

Instead:

$$
\boxed{
\mathcal K
\longrightarrow
\mathfrak E_{\mathcal K}
\longrightarrow
\mathfrak P(\mathfrak E_{\mathcal K})
}
$$

Potentially:

$$
I^*(Q,\Gamma)
\in
\mathfrak E_{\mathcal K}
$$

or, if the ideal epistemic state is probabilistic,

$$
\boxed{
\mu^*(Q,\Gamma)
\in
\mathfrak P(\mathfrak E_{\mathcal K}).
}
$$

That gives us a very clean separation:

```text
                    KNOWLEDGEOS KERNEL
                           │
                invariant boundary
                           │
                           ▼
                 𝔈_K admissible
                epistemic state space
                           │
                 probability structure?
                           │
                           ▼
                 𝓟(𝔈_K)
             probabilistic epistemic
                    state space
                           │
                           ▼
              ideal state μ*(Q,Γ)
```

The probability space is therefore a **possible mathematical structure over the admissible state space**, not the Kernel itself.

