# 9. One thing I would change immediately in the old roadmap

The September document says:

> “Stop discovering. Start closing.” 

I would now change that principle.

Because of your corpus-first methodology, the correct principle is:

$$
\boxed{
\textbf{Stop promoting. Start deriving and falsifying.}
}
$$

We don't want to “close” concepts because they appear complete.

We want:

$$
\boxed{
\text{Candidate}
\rightarrow
\text{formalization}
\rightarrow
\text{counterexample}
\rightarrow
\text{reduction}
\rightarrow
\text{proof}
\rightarrow
\text{closure}
}
$$

That is much more rigorous.

